//
// Description: This script shows how to read a device and evaulate the return automatically by definng the correct output
//
// 
// - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -

[0] force FAIL by default to avoid IMPORTANT message below.
#1: Connect to equipment
CLICK_OK:
CONNECT: MLPRO2 
COMMAND: MLPRO2 If#	// turn off any LEDs still on: 
IF_NOT:
GOTO: #1


#2: READAMPS
COMMAND: MLPRO2 READAMPS
CLICK_OK:
READLINE: MLPRO2 READAMPS
Returned Version is = %READAMPS%
CLICK_OK:

#3: Full load test - 4 output on at the same time 
COMMAND: MLPRO2 RING 001111 1023
CLICK_OK:
COMMAND: MLPRO2 READAMPS
READLINE: MLPRO2 READAMPS
Returned Version is = %READAMPS%
CLICK_OK:
RANGE: %READAMPS% 950 50					// PASS if result is between 900 and 950
IF:
GOTO: #3.1: 
The returned result is NOT as exected, investigate the fault and click RETRY to repeat the test.
.
.
The expected result is not as expected.
IMPORTANT: Test has FAILED                Test has FAILED                   Test has FAILED                   Test has FAILED
COMMENT: If you want to continue fault-finding the rest of the PCB, click on ‘Skip’
SKIP_FAIL: #3
GOTO: #4


#4: Test complete:
COMMAND: MLPRO2 If#	// turn off any LEDs still on: 
a. All tests instructions have been completed and a log file created.
b. Click OK to finish and then power off the PSU and disconnect the PCB.
CLICK_OK:

#QUIT:
COMMAND: MLPRO2 If#	// turn off any LEDs still on: 
DISCONNECT: MLPRO2
SAVE_LOG: